{"candidates":[{"content":"Kind: Contradiction. The preference for better-corroborated theories (SRC_003) contradicts the claim that such preference smuggles induction (SRC_001) if the 'critical attitude' is strictly a logical report of past error elimination with zero normative force for future action. Refuted If: Any agent acting on the preference demonstrates an expectation of future reliability, thereby converting the methodological rule into an inductive premise.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"a15f4b263b9598e290bb50f8612ea5e31dd02988e16e61a29a969e35df8d58d4"},{"role":"dependence","target":"05e7096fadd9de5d7aabfc9b52de4f1726e6a9a642508e3717f9769dc2afada0"}],"typicality":0.95},{"content":"Kind: Dependence. The defense of the preference as a 'critical rationality' decision rule (SRC_003) depends on the failure of the 'smuggling induction' accusation (SRC_005) to prove that pragmatic action requires probabilistic belief. Refuted If: It is demonstrated that all pragmatic decisions inherently assign subjective probability, making the 'non-inductive' label semantically empty.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"05e7096fadd9de5d7aabfc9b52de4f1726e6a9a642508e3717f9769dc2afada0"},{"role":"dependence","target":"c82de43e800f8bbc17546a615b1105f004ddc362f858f8ec10422042fbb14ab3"}],"typicality":0.88},{"content":"Kind: Abstraction. The concept of 'verisimilitude' in SRC_004 acts as an abstraction of the 'uniformity of nature' assumption in SRC_002, attempting to retain predictive utility without the metaphysical commitment. Refuted If: Verisimilitude cannot be defined or measured without implicitly invoking the very uniformity principle it seeks to abstract away.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"28c31d36f3430bfcde886ac08aadcea30b09e07f6b2366ee442e43527f4697bb"},{"role":"dependence","target":"4dfcde0c96c46f06c4ca5541463ed52b1212f826d2abb071a6fca11fb3227d9b"}],"typicality":0.75},{"content":"Kind: Shared